  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Energy entrepreneur Sam Nappi commissioned World Harmony Studios to accommodate music, theatre and film work in a redwood lodge in upstate New York. He selected acoustic designer John Storyk after their first meeting. Storyk's team used glass walls and specially treated windows to preserve views and visibility between recording rooms. The Syracuse Symphony recorded the studio's first session.\n\nNappi and his wife, Carol, also initiated a competition pairing researchers from Syracuse University and SUNY Upstate Medical University. When finalists presented their proposals, the couple increased the funding on the day, allowing additional collaborative projects to receive support.",
    "html": "<p>Energy entrepreneur Sam Nappi commissioned World Harmony Studios to accommodate music, theatre and film work in a redwood lodge in upstate New York. He selected acoustic designer John Storyk after their first meeting. Storyk's team used glass walls and specially treated windows to preserve views and visibility between recording rooms. The Syracuse Symphony recorded the studio's first session.</p>\r\n<p>Nappi and his wife, Carol, also initiated a competition pairing researchers from Syracuse University and SUNY Upstate Medical University. When finalists presented their proposals, the couple increased the funding on the day, allowing additional collaborative projects to receive support.</p>\r\n",
